# Keep the build context to exactly what the images need. Two reasons, one of
# them load-bearing: `.env` and `secrets/` would otherwise be sent to the
# daemon and become one `COPY .` away from living in a published image layer.
#
# scripts/package-deploy.js scans the assembled artifact for credential
# material and refuses to package a hit, so this file is the first of two
# defences rather than the only one.

.env
.env.*
secrets/
*.pem
*.key

# Local state that is not an input to any image. `artifact/` IS an input (both
# Dockerfiles copy from it) and is deliberately not listed here; sourcemaps
# never reach it because packaging does not copy them.
node_modules/
.DS_Store

# Docs and scripts are read by humans, not by the daemon.
README.md
nodegx-deploy.sh
